          "question": "What sort of dietary change does guidance describe for high blood pressure?",
          "answer": "Authoritative guidance recommends several dietary changes for managing high blood pressure, whether or not medication is also used. These include:\n\n*   Reducing dietary sodium.\n*   Adopting a dietary pattern rich in vegetables, fruit, whole grains, and low-fat dairy.\n*   Choosing foods low in saturated fat.\n\nThese recommendations come from \"Major cardiology society consensus guidance\" as summarized in `guideline-hypertension-first-line-treatment`. Each of these changes can lead to a meaningful reduction in blood pressure on its own, and their effects are partly additive when combined.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
